.TH zork1 1 "FUZIX Games" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
zork1 \- Zork I: The Great Underground Empire
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zork1
.RB [ \-t ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Infocom's Zork I, by Marc Blank, Dave Lebling, Bruce Daniels and Tim
Anderson, in its final release of 1988.  You start west of a white house
with a boarded front door, and the treasures of the Great Underground
Empire are somewhere below it.
.PP
Unlike the older adventures, Zork understands whole sentences:
.BR "open the mailbox" ,
.BR "put the egg in the case" ,
.BR "take all but the lamp" .
.B look
describes where you are,
.B inventory
or
.B i
lists what you carry, and
.B score
says how you are doing, out of 350.
.B save
and
.B restore
keep a game in a file, asking for its name, and
.B quit
ends it.
.PP
The options are
.BR z3 's,
which plays the game.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/games/lib/zork1.z3
The story file, release 119, serial 880429.
.TP
.B /usr/games/lib/zork1.LICENSE
Microsoft released Zork I under the MIT licence in 2025; this is the
licence, which comes with the game.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR z3 (1),
.BR advent (1)
